{"name":"Paperback Chic","title":"Paperback Chic","revision":236497,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Paperback_Chic","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Paperback Chic is a simplified design style prevalent between the late 2010s and present that features natural, soft colors, playful or retro airy layouts and display fonts that gives modern product labeling/packaging and branding a friendly, wholesome, and artistic paperback-book look where they appear everywhere from trendy food package labels to wellness drinks. It is often used by cafes and organic food brands to appeal to a general market."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"list","text":"Matte Textures: Labeling product surfaces that are meant to feel tactile, organic, and down-to-earth."},{"kind":"list","text":"Open Layouts: Lots of white space with friendly, hand-drawn, or simple illustrations."},{"kind":"list","text":"Fun Fonts: retro serif, wavy, or didone display typefaces that influence a vintage-styled look."},{"kind":"list","text":"Soft/Light Colors: Earthy creams, warm pastel tones, sage greens, and muted terracotta."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Brands"},{"kind":"list","text":"Craftmix"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rite N' Lite"},{"kind":"list","text":"Chobani"},{"kind":"list","text":"Olipop"},{"kind":"list","text":"Gelato Fiasco"},{"kind":"list","text":"La Canette"},{"kind":"list","text":"Core & Rind"},{"kind":"list","text":"Onda"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kindfull"},{"kind":"list","text":"Meridian"},{"kind":"list","text":"Spindrift"}],"contentStatus":"full-source","images":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/4/43/6767676767hahaha676767.webp/revision/latest?cb=20260816130447","caption":"6767676767hahaha676767","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:6767676767hahaha676767.webp","remote":true,"local":"images/det